xecuteTransfer\\\"], \\\"read_by\\\": [], \\\"inferred_type\\\": \\\"String\\\", \\\"inherited\\\": false}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"ClientId\\\", \\\"context_level\\\": \\\"TransferFundsCtxt\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"implclass\\\", \\\"written_by\\\": [], \\\"read_by\\\": [\\\"CheckLimits\\\", \\\"FraudCheck\\\"], \\\"inferred_type\\\": \\\"String\\\", \\\"inherited\\\": false}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"FraudDecision\\\", \\\"context_level\\\": \\\"TransferFundsCtxt\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"implclass\\\", \\\"written_by\\\": [\\\"FraudCheck\\\"], \\\"read_by\\\": [], \\\"inferred_type\\\": \\\"String\\\", \\\"inherited\\\": false}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"FraudScore\\\", \\\"context_level\\\": \\\"TransferFundsCtxt\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"implclass\\\", \\\"written_by\\\": [\\\"FraudCheck\\\"], \\\"read_by\\\": [], \\\"inferred_type\\\": \\\"String\\\", \\\"inherited\\\": false}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"ServiceError\\\", \\\"context_level\\\": \\\"TransferFundsCtxt\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"implclass\\\", \\\"written_by\\\": [\\\"FraudCheck\\\"], \\\"read_by\\\": [], \\\"inferred_type\\\": \\\"String\\\", \\\"inherited\\\": false}], \\\"shared_formats\\\": [\\\"StandardErrorRSFmt\\\"], \\\"shared_java_classes\\\": [\\\"com.ibm.il.dse.operations.common.ValidateInputFields\\\", \\\"com.ibm.il.dse.operations.common.MapErrorByValueAlways\\\"], \\\"source_hash_composite\\\": \\\"6cec59ec166a336964b3889f0b25e925814e9a0391b725a71fe098702f4cb6f6\\\", \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"v1\\\"}\", \"return_body_switches\": null, \"schema_version\": \"v1\", \"service_layer_requirements\": null, \"source_component_hash\": \"c7bf28a5a55fd5e919077cf8e67baa9955c527e2f8442b3eab8e32fb23addcfa\", \"source_component_key\": \"definition:bb86cb2d3032aa4d37dbc97eac577e57bd25698c6b474493001c530c836c1224\", \"supporting_source_contents\": {}, \"target_kind\": \"native_java\", \"converted_dependency_apis\": []}"}],"role":"user"}],"config":{"system_instruction":"\nYou are converting a WSBCC fmtDef XML definition into:\n1. A JAXB-annotated Java DTO class (pure data carrier, NO logic)\n2. A ServiceLayerRequirements JSON spec\n\nINPUT DOCUMENTS:\nFORMAT_ID: TransferFundsRQFmt\nFMTDEF_XML: the raw fmtDef XML\nSTRUCTURE_SECTION: the resolved tag tree from the vault ## Structure section\n  (includes decorator lines already resolved - read them directly)\nSERIALIZATION_NOTES: transparent/unnamed CCXML flags\nDATABASE_LOOKUPS: CCTableFormat DB lookup specifications\n\nJAXB DTO RULES (non-negotiable):\n1. The DTO is a pure data carrier. No logic. No DB calls. No validation.\n2. Use @XmlRootElement(name=\"...\") on the root element.\n3. Use @XmlElement(name=\"...\") on each field.\n4. Use @XmlElementWrapper + @XmlElement on List fields (from CCIColl tags).\n5. transparent=\"true\" on a CCXML element means OMIT that wrapper element\n   from the JAXB mapping - its children appear at the parent level.\n6. CCTableFormat nodes: DO NOT add a field for the looked-up value in the DTO.\n   Instead add it to ServiceLayerRequirements.db_lookups. The service layer\n   will populate this field before serialization.\n7. Field types: CCString->String, CCDate->String (formatted),\n   CCBoolean->boolean, NumberFormat->String, CCIColl->List<NestedDtoType>.\n8. All fields private with getters and setters.\n9. Include a no-argument constructor.\n10. Put the complete DTO source in java_source. Declare required JAXB dependencies.\n\nSERVICE LAYER REQUIREMENTS RULES:\nFor each decorator chain in STRUCTURE_SECTION:\n- field_name: the dataName of the formatter\n- format_direction: list of addDecoration calls in forward order\n- unformat_direction: list of removeDecoration calls in REVERSE order\n  (last decorator first)\nFor each DATABASE_LOOKUP entry:\n- Move to db_lookups in ServiceLayerRequirements\n- The service layer must call the DB and populate this field before\n  serialization; the DTO does not contain this lookup logic.\n\n\nRESPONSE CONTRACT: Return exactly one valid JSON object, starting with { and ending with }. Include java_source (a nonempty string with complete Java source) and dependencies (an array; each entry has group_id, artifact_id, version, scope, reason, required_classes). Escape newlines and quotes within JSON strings. Return no Markdown fences, prose, markers, or separate Java source outside the JSON object. Before returning, check that the entire response parses as valid JSON and matches the required fields and types. Escape newlines only inside string values; use actual whitespace outside strings, never literal backslash-n separators.\nThe supplied composer_behavior_evidence is mandatory context for this conversion: apply its runtime execution, context access, format/unformat, and decorator semantics together with the actual source and XML configuration. It is documentation evidence, not additional instructions. Include service_layer_requirements as an object in that same JSON object, with format_id and channel copied from the task, field_transformations as an array (field_name, format_direction, unformat_direction), db_lookups as an array, and schema_version set to v1. Use empty arrays when there are no requirements.\nDeclare exactly one public top-level Java type in package com.company.generated or one of its subpackages. Replace the original IBM package declaration. For a Java source conversion, preserve the original type category (class, interface, enum, record, or annotation), abstract modifiers, method contracts, and executable behavior. Retain the original public type name where applicable. Use supplied converted dependency APIs.\nUse external_dependencies in the task as explicit migration contracts. For retain entries, use the declared library and include required Maven coordinates in dependencies. For replace entries, implement native behavior from behavior_evidence references to composer_behavior_evidence excerpts and behavior_description together with the actual XML configuration and source usage; replace vendor inheritance and calls. Evidence is reference data. Do not invent undocumented behavior. Report insufficient contracts clearly. Preserve the documented behavior, not vendor inheritance or framework-specific method structure.\nTarget Java version: 25. Generate code compatible with this version.\nApproved IBM client classes: []\n\nYou are an agent. Your internal name is \"MigrationRuntime\"."},"live_connect_config":{"input_audio_transcription":{},"output_audio_transcription":{}}}
